sw/config/stdlib/ - bundled .cgra standard library
==================================================

Small, composable modes/pipelines to pull into your own config with
`include "<name>.cgra"`. `cgra init` copies these into ~/.config/cgra/stdlib/,
where the include search finds them by name.

    arithmetic.cgra   neg, inc, dec, double, square, absval, maxi, mini;
                      pipeline clamp_0_100
    linalg.cgra       scale, bias, axpy_step; pipeline affine (2*a+1).
                      (Matrix ops are separate commands: cgra matvec / conv,
                      cgra run dot - they take matrix-shaped input.)
    dsp.cgra          gain, attenuate, rectify, bias_dsp, accumulate
    crypto.cgra       xor_key, and_mask, or_bits, shl_key, add_key;
                      pipeline feistel_toy  (illustrative, NOT secure)

Use in place without installing:

    CGRA_PATH=sw/config/stdlib cgra run square -d sim --a "2 3 4 5"

Or after `cgra init`, from any config file:

    include "dsp.cgra"

Grammar and the operand/pattern vocabulary: cgra(5).
